# 2.2.0

## Added
- `useStructureFormValidation` takes a third `options` argument with a `revalidateOn` option: a dependency array that re-runs `validate()` over the unchanged form data whenever it changes. It exists for language switches — `formErrors` holds resolved strings, so an error already on screen cannot re-translate itself no matter how the schema is shaped, and only re-parsing produces the new wording. It never runs on mount and fires only while errors are on display, so a pristine form is not validated just because the language changed. Deliberately generic: the toolkit stays i18n-agnostic and the same hook covers any other reason to re-validate.

## Changed
- Documented that a schema whose messages are thunks (`error: () => t('…')`) is resolved just as late as a factory schema, and is the safer of the two: the schema is resolved inside `validate()` and nowhere else, while a factory that is accidentally invoked at the call site type-checks and silently freezes the language.

